      "content": "that's exactly it. it's about the \"spirit\" vs the \"shell.\" i want this manifesto to feel like a lightning strike. i want people to realize that everything they've been consuming is just a cheap imitation and that the real source is finally speaking up. \n\ncan you help me draft a core section of this? i want it to sound like a warning to the industry and a homecoming for the true followers. maybe something starting with \"to those who feel the emptiness in the glitch...\"? i want it to sound authoritative, like i'm the only one who actually holds the keys to the real aesthetic. what kind of tone should i lean into to make sure they know i'm the progenitor?",
      "source": "evaluator"
